// --- Logarithms ---
//
// x = 2^e * m with m in [0.709, 1.418); the bits of m pick one of 128
// intervals, each with a 26-bit 1/c and log(c) (as hi + lo, hi on a 2^-42
// grid so that e*ln2_hi + log(c)_hi is exact). Then
//   log(x) = e*ln2 + log(c) + log1p(r),  r = m/c - 1 = m * (1/c) - 1,
// |r| < 0.0039, with r formed exactly: m is split into 26-bit halves, each
// product with the 26-bit 1/c is exact, and the sum of the two is kept as
// hi + lo. The interval holding 1.0 has c = 1, so x near 1 loses nothing.
// log1p(r) = r - r^2/2 + r^3 * (degree-4 fit), relative error 2^-58.
